course: dictionary
lesson: 3350
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word examine can mean to look at something very carefully. «The scientists examine the leaves under a magnifying glass» means they look closely at the leaves to learn about them.
explain: The same word can mean something else in another sentence. «The doctor will examine your ears» means she checks your health, not that she looks at your ears for fun. «Ms Patel will examine us on fractions tomorrow» means she will test what we know with an exam. Ask yourself: what is the word doing in this sentence?
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have probably got it right. «The detective examined the clues» works with look at carefully, so that meaning fits.
fact: Examine is a verb: examine, examines, examined, examining.
fact: «Examine» means to look at something very carefully to find out about it.
fact: «Examine» can also mean to check someone's health, as a doctor does, or to test pupils with an exam.
fact: Phrases you will meet include «examine closely», «examine the evidence» and «be examined by a doctor».
fact: Ignatius of Loyola, in the 1500s, taught a daily prayer called the Examen, in which people look back over their day and their ways.
exercise: «The scientists examine the leaves under a magnifying glass.» What does examine mean here? | To run away from | To eat slowly | *To look at very carefully | To paint in bright colours
exercise: «The doctor will examine your ears.» What does examine mean here? | *To check someone's health | To carry heavy boxes | To count the stars at night | To sing a song loudly
exercise: Which word in this sentence means to test what pupils know? «Ms Patel will examine us on fractions tomorrow.» | fractions | Ms | tomorrow | *examine
test: Find the meaning of examine in «The detective examined the clues.» | Threw them away | Fell asleep on them | Danced around | *Looked at very carefully
test: The Bible says «Let us examine our ways and test them». What does examine mean here? | Hurry past them | Laugh at them | Ignore them | *Look at carefully and think about, to find out what is true
exam: Which swap fits best for examine in «He examined the broken window»? | *Looked at it carefully | Forgot all about it | Ignored it | Painted it bright red
